# Obsidian per-machine UI/workspace state — not portable vault content
.obsidian/

# Derived semantic-recall index (rebuildable via engine/bin/rag-build.sh)
.rag/

# Drainable upkeep queue + lock (rebuildable via engine/bin/upkeep.sh scan)
.upkeep/

# Transient engine-proposal outbox (scratch handoff blocks; not a vault node)
.engine-proposal/

# Auto-captured session buffer (rag-capture.sh, SessionEnd). Per-machine scratch, not
# vault content: the blocks hold this machine's absolute transcript paths and local repo
# HEADs, which mean nothing on another machine. Tracking it also deadlocked the workflow
# — the hook necessarily writes to the CANONICAL checkout (by SessionEnd the session's
# worktree is already gc'd), so a tracked buffer left canonical permanently dirty and the
# next session's `integrate` refused. The monthly files are ignored; raw/sessions/.gitkeep
# stays tracked so the node folder still ships.
raw/sessions/*.md

# Foreign-boundary denylist for lint.sh's gate. Git-ignored ON PURPOSE: the file
# names the OTHER boundary's identifiers, so tracking it would commit exactly what
# the gate exists to keep out of this vault. Per-machine; an absent file reports
# "not armed" rather than passing silently.
.wiki-gates.local

# OS cruft
.DS_Store

# Per-machine engine adoption marker (apply-adopt.sh): it records `git describe` of
# the pinned engine for THIS checkout, so committing it would publish one machine's
# adoption state to every other machine — and the fast path would then read a marker
# that describes a different machine. apply-adopt.sh's header has always called this
# file "per-machine, gitignored"; this line is what actually makes that true.
.engine-adopted

# The vault's write-time gate, installed by adoption. IGNORED ON PURPOSE, and this is
# a decision rather than an oversight — the alternative is defensible, so leaving it
# unstated meant each vault resolved it by accident.
#
# Installation stays per-machine and add-only: adoption never overwrites a hook the
# vault wrote, and a vault that tracked its hook would keep whatever template it first
# adopted, forever, with no upgrade path. Gate CORRECTNESS does not depend on this
# either way — core.hooksPath is written as an ABSOLUTE path (v1.35.0) precisely so it
# resolves from every linked worktree whether or not .githooks/ is tracked.
#
# A vault that already tracks .githooks/ keeps tracking it: this line only affects
# untracked files, and adoption does not change a state a vault is already in.
.githooks/

# Per-session worktree parent (vault-worktree.sh). Engine-created and identical on
# every machine, so it belongs in the tracked ignore file. It used to be hidden only
# via .git/info/exclude, which is per-checkout and never cloned — so a second machine
# showed it as untracked until that machine happened to run a worktree verb. The
# exclude write is kept as a belt for vaults that have not yet reconciled.
.worktrees/
